    turnFlow: "Deal and pass as in standard Hearts: all 52 cards dealt one at a time (13 each); each player passes three cards in a rotating cycle (left, right, across, no pass). After the pass, each player may place one of the four special cards face up in front of them (turbo-charge). The holder of the 2 of clubs leads it to the first trick. Players must follow suit if possible; highest card of the suit led wins the trick. Hearts may not be led until a heart has been played to a previous trick (hearts broken) or the leader holds only hearts. A turbo-charged card may not be played the first time that suit is led. Turbo-charged Queen of Spades or Jack of Diamonds doubles that card's value; turbo-charged Ace of Hearts doubles all hearts for that hand; turbo-charged Ten of Clubs quadruples the hand score for the player who captures it. Shooting the moon: capture all penalty cards to deduct 26 from your score or add 26 to everyone else's.",
